(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the mathematical expressions for RMS value, Average value, Form Factor, and Crest Factor of a pure sinusoidal waveform.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Derivation of Sinusoidal Waveform Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   1. Root-Mean-Square \(RMS / Effective\) Value:) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as the steady DC current/voltage that produces the identical thermal dissipation in a) Tj
T*
(   given resistor over a full period T:) Tj
T*
(   V_rms = sqrt\( \(1 / T\) * Integral_0^T [v\(t\)]^2 dt \).) Tj
T*
(   - For v\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t\) with T = 2*pi / omega:) Tj
T*
(   V_rms^2 = \(1 / 2*pi\) * Integral_0^{2*pi} Vm^2 * sin^2\(theta\) d\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Using identity sin^2\(theta\) = [1 - cos\(2*theta\)] / 2:) Tj
T*
(   V_rms^2 = \(Vm^2 / 4*pi\) * [ theta - sin\(2*theta\)/2 ]_0^{2*pi} = \(Vm^2 / 4*pi\) * \(2*pi\) = Vm^2 /) Tj
T*
(   2.) Tj
T*
(   V_rms = Vm / sqrt\(2\) approx 0.7071 * Vm.) Tj
T*
(   2. Average Value \(over a positive half-cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   - Over a full symmetric cycle, net area is zero. Average value is evaluated over half-cycle) Tj
T*
(   T/2:) Tj
T*
(   V_avg = \(1 / pi\) * Integral_0^pi Vm * sin\(theta\) d\(theta\) = \(Vm / pi\) * [ -cos\(theta\) ]_0^pi =) Tj
T*
(   \(Vm / pi\) * [-\(-1\) - \(-1\)] = 2 * Vm / pi approx 0.6366 * Vm.) Tj
T*
(   3. Form Factor \(k_f\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as the ratio of RMS value to Average value:) Tj
T*
(   k_f = V_rms / V_avg = [Vm / sqrt\(2\)] / [2 * Vm / pi] = pi / \(2 * sqrt\(2\)\) approx 1.1107.) Tj
T*
(   4. Crest \(Peak\) Factor \(k_a\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as the ratio of Peak value to RMS value:) Tj
T*
(   k_a = V_peak / V_rms = Vm / [Vm / sqrt\(2\)] = sqrt\(2\) approx 1.4142.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the steady-state behavior of pure R, pure L, and pure C elements subjected to sinusoidal excitation, deriving impedance, phase, and power.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sinusoidal AC Response of Pure Circuit Elements:) Tj
T*
(   1. Pure Resistive Element \(R\):) Tj
T*
(   - Applied voltage: v\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - By Ohm's law: i\(t\) = v\(t\) / R = \(Vm / R\) * sin\(omega * t\) = Im * sin\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Angle: phi = 0 degrees \(Voltage and current are perfectly in phase\).) Tj
T*
(   - Impedance: Z_R = R + j0 = R /_ 0 deg.) Tj
T*
(   - Power: p\(t\) = v\(t\)*i\(t\) = Vm*Im * sin^2\(omega*t\) = \(Vm*Im / 2\) * [1 - cos\(2*omega*t\)].) Tj
T*
(   Average Power: P = V_rms * I_rms \(all converted into heat\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Pure Inductive Element \(L\):) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage: v\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t\) = L * di/dt => di = \(Vm / L\) * sin\(omega * t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating: i\(t\) = - \(Vm / omega*L\) * cos\(omega * t\) = Im * sin\(omega * t - pi/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Angle: Current lags applied voltage by strictly 90 degrees \(pi/2 radians\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reactance and Impedance: XL = omega * L = 2*pi*f*L; Z_L = j*XL = XL /_ 90 deg.) Tj
T*
(   - Power: p\(t\) = Vm*Im * sin\(omega*t\) * [-cos\(omega*t\)] = - \(Vm*Im / 2\) * sin\(2*omega*t\).) Tj
T*
(   Average Power: P_avg = 0 W. Pure reactive energy exchange with magnetic field.) Tj
T*
(   3. Pure Capacitive Element \(C\):) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage: v\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t\). Charge q\(t\) = C * v\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Current: i\(t\) = dq/dt = C * d/dt [Vm * sin\(omega * t\)] = omega * C * Vm * cos\(omega * t\) = Im) Tj
T*
(   * sin\(omega * t + pi/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Angle: Current leads applied voltage by strictly 90 degrees \(pi/2 radians\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
