(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the complete impedance, current, phasor diagram, and Power Triangle relationships for a series R-L-C AC circuit.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Complete Analysis of Series R-L-C AC Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   1. Differential Equation and Phasor Representation:) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit contains resistor R, inductor L, and capacitor C in series excited by v\(t\) = Vm *) Tj
T*
(   sin\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - KVL in time domain: v\(t\) = R * i\(t\) + L * di/dt + \(1/C\) * Integral\(i dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Transforming into Phasor Domain:) Tj
T*
(   V = V_R + V_L + V_C = I * R + I * \(j * XL\) + I * \(-j * XC\) = I * [ R + j * \(XL - XC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Complex Impedance:) Tj
T*
(   - Z = R + j * \(XL - XC\) = |Z| /_ phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Magnitude: |Z| = sqrt\( R^2 + \(XL - XC\)^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Angle: phi = arctan\( \(XL - XC\) / R \).) Tj
T*
(   - Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   * Inductive \(XL > XC\): phi > 0, current lags voltage by angle phi.) Tj
T*
(   * Capacitive \(XC > XL\): phi < 0, current leads voltage by angle |phi|.) Tj
T*
(   * Resonance \(XL = XC\): phi = 0, |Z| = R, current is purely in phase.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Power Triangle:) Tj
T*
(   - Apparent Power S \(VA\): S = V_rms * I_rms = I_rms^2 * |Z|.) Tj
T*
(   - Active \(Real\) Power P \(Watts\): P = V_rms * I_rms * cos\(phi\) = I_rms^2 * R.) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive Power Q \(VAR\): Q = V_rms * I_rms * sin\(phi\) = I_rms^2 * \(XL - XC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Geometric Vector Relation:) Tj
T*
(   S = P + j * Q => |S| = sqrt\(P^2 + Q^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Power Factor: cos\(phi\) = P / |S| = R / |Z|.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the resonant frequency, quality factor, bandwidth, and voltage magnification of a Series R-L-C Resonant Circuit.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Series Resonance in R-L-C Circuits:) Tj
T*
(   1. Resonant Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Resonance occurs when the net imaginary reactance vanishes: X_net = XL - XC = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - omega_0 * L - 1 / \(omega_0 * C\) = 0 => omega_0^2 = 1 / \(L * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Resonant Angular Frequency: omega_0 = 1 / sqrt\(L * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Resonant Frequency in Hertz: f_0 = 1 / [2 * pi * sqrt\(L * C\)].) Tj
T*
(   2. Impedance and Current at Resonance:) Tj
T*
(   - Z_0 = R + j0 = R \(Minimum possible impedance\).) Tj
T*
(   - Current: I_0 = V / R \(Maximum possible current, strictly in phase with supply voltage, cos) Tj
T*
(   phi = 1.0\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Quality Factor \(Q-Factor\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as 2*pi * \(Maximum energy stored / Energy dissipated per cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   Q = omega_0 * L / R = 1 / \(omega_0 * C * R\) = \(1 / R\) * sqrt\(L / C\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Voltage Magnification:) Tj
T*
(   - At resonance, current I_0 = V / R.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage across inductor: V_L = I_0 * XL = \(V / R\) * \(omega_0 * L\) = Q * V.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage across capacitor: V_C = I_0 * XC = \(V / R\) * \(1 / omega_0 * C\) = Q * V.) Tj
T*
(   - For high-Q circuits \(e.g., Q = 50\), inductor and capacitor voltages can reach 50 times the) Tj
T*
ET

