BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Parallel Resonant Circuit \(Tank Circuit with coil resistance\), deriving resonant frequency and dynamic impedance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Parallel Resonance \(Practical Tank Circuit\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Model:) Tj
T*
(   - An inductive branch having resistance R and inductance L in parallel with a pure capacitive) Tj
T*
(   branch C.) Tj
T*
(   - Branch 1 admittance: Y1 = 1 / \(R + j*XL\) = \(R - j*XL\) / \(R^2 + XL^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Branch 2 admittance: Y2 = j * omega * C.) Tj
T*
(   - Total circuit admittance:) Tj
T*
(   Y = Y1 + Y2 = [ R / \(R^2 + XL^2\) ] + j * [ omega * C - XL / \(R^2 + XL^2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Condition for Antiresonance \(Unity Power Factor\):) Tj
T*
(   - Set net susceptance to zero:) Tj
T*
(   omega_r * C - \(omega_r * L\) / \(R^2 + omega_r^2 * L^2\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Dividing by omega_r * C:) Tj
T*
(   R^2 + omega_r^2 * L^2 = L / C => omega_r^2 * L^2 = \(L / C\) - R^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Resonant Angular Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   omega_r = sqrt\( 1/\(L * C\) - R^2 / L^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Condition for Resonance: \(L / C\) > R^2 => R < sqrt\(L / C\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Dynamic Impedance \(Z_dyn\):) Tj
T*
(   - At resonance, Y is purely real \(conductance\):) Tj
T*
(   Y_r = R / \(R^2 + omega_r^2 * L^2\) = R / \(L / C\) = \(C * R\) / L.) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamic Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   Z_dyn = 1 / Y_r = L / \(C * R\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because R is typically small, Z_dyn is very large \(hundreds of kOhms\).) Tj
T*
(   - Current drawn from the AC source is minimal: I_min = V / Z_dyn = V * C * R / L.) Tj
T*
(   - Functions as an effective Rejector Circuit in RF tuners and amplifiers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
