(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the mathematical relationships between Line and Phase quantities in a Balanced Star \(Y\) Connected 3-Phase System.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Balanced Star \(Wye\) Connected 3-Phase System:) Tj
T*
(   1. Configuration and Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Three identical coils connected to a common neutral point N. Terminals are R, Y, B.) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Voltages \(Neutral-to-Line\): V_RN, V_YN, V_BN with equal magnitude V_ph, mutually) Tj
T*
(   displaced by 120 degrees:) Tj
T*
(   V_RN = V_ph /_ 0 deg.) Tj
T*
(   V_YN = V_ph /_ -120 deg.) Tj
T*
(   V_BN = V_ph /_ -240 deg \(+120 deg\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Line Voltages \(Line-to-Line\):) Tj
T*
(   - By KVL, line voltage V_RY between lines R and Y:) Tj
T*
(   V_RY = V_RN - V_YN = V_ph /_ 0 deg - V_ph /_ -120 deg.) Tj
T*
