(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Theory of Two-Wattmeter Power Measurement:) Tj
T*
(   1. Connection Scheme:) Tj
T*
(   - Current coils \(CC\) of Wattmeters W1 and W2 are inserted in lines R and B respectively.) Tj
T*
(   - Pressure coils \(PC\) are connected between lines R-Y and lines B-Y respectively \(line Y serves) Tj
T*
(   as common reference\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Wattmeter Reading Equations:) Tj
T*
(   - Wattmeter 1: Measures instantaneous product of line current I_R and voltage across its PC) Tj
T*
(   \(V_RY\).) Tj
T*
(   Phasor V_RY leads V_RN by 30 deg. If phase current I_R lags V_RN by load angle phi, angle) Tj
T*
(   between V_RY and I_R is \(30 deg - phi\).) Tj
T*
(   W1 = |V_RY| * |I_R| * cos\(30 deg - phi\) = V_L * I_L * cos\(30 deg - phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Wattmeter 2: Measures product of line current I_B and voltage across its PC \(V_BY = -V_YB\).) Tj
T*
(   Angle between V_BY and I_B is \(30 deg + phi\).) Tj
T*
(   W2 = |V_BY| * |I_B| * cos\(30 deg + phi\) = V_L * I_L * cos\(30 deg + phi\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Sum of Readings \(Total 3-Phase Power\):) Tj
T*
(   - W1 + W2 = V_L * I_L * [ cos\(30 - phi\) + cos\(30 + phi\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Using identity cos\(A - B\) + cos\(A + B\) = 2 * cos\(A\) * cos\(B\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 + W2 = V_L * I_L * [ 2 * cos\(30 deg\) * cos\(phi\) ] = V_L * I_L * [ 2 * \(sqrt\(3\)/2\) * cos\(phi\)) Tj
T*
(   ] = sqrt\(3\) * V_L * I_L * cos\(phi\) = Total Active Power P.) Tj
T*
(   4. Difference of Readings and Power Factor Determination:) Tj
T*
(   - W1 - W2 = V_L * I_L * [ cos\(30 - phi\) - cos\(30 + phi\) ] = V_L * I_L * [ 2 * sin\(30 deg\) *) Tj
T*
(   sin\(phi\) ] = V_L * I_L * sin\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Dividing difference by sum:) Tj
T*
(   \(W1 - W2\) / \(W1 + W2\) = [ V_L * I_L * sin\(phi\) ] / [ sqrt\(3\) * V_L * I_L * cos\(phi\) ] =) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) / sqrt\(3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thus: tan\(phi\) = sqrt\(3\) * \(W1 - W2\) / \(W1 + W2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Load Power Factor: cos\(phi\) = cos\( arctan[ sqrt\(3\) * \(W1 - W2\) / \(W1 + W2\) ] \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
