/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the transient growth and decay of current in a series R-L circuit excited by a constant DC voltage source.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   DC Transient Analysis of Series R-L Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   1. Current Growth \(Energization\):) Tj
T*
(   - Switch closes at t = 0 connecting DC source V across series R and L. Initial current i\(0-\) =) Tj
T*
(   0.) Tj
T*
(   - KVL differential equation:) Tj
T*
(   L * di/dt + R * i\(t\) = V => di/dt + \(R / L\) * i\(t\) = V / L.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating factor method: IF = exp\( Integral \(R/L\) dt \) = exp\(R*t / L\).) Tj
T*
(   d/dt [ i * exp\(R*t / L\) ] = \(V / L\) * exp\(R*t / L\).) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating:) Tj
T*
(   i\(t\) * exp\(R*t / L\) = \(V / R\) * exp\(R*t / L\) + K.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying initial condition i\(0\) = 0: 0 = V/R + K => K = -V/R.) Tj
T*
(   - Final Growth Equation:) Tj
T*
(   i\(t\) = \(V / R\) * [ 1 - exp\(- t / tau\) ], where tau = L / R is the inductive time constant.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = tau: i\(tau\) = \(V/R\) * \(1 - e^-1\) = 0.6321 * \(V/R\) \(63.2% of steady state\).) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage across inductor: v_L\(t\) = L * di/dt = V * exp\(- t / tau\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Current Decay \(De-energization\):) Tj
T*
(   - At steady state, i\(0\) = I0 = V/R. Source is disconnected and circuit shorted at t = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - KVL: L * di/dt + R * i = 0 => di / i = - \(R / L\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Solution: i\(t\) = I0 * exp\(- t / tau\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stored magnetic energy E = 0.5 * L * I0^2 is fully dissipated as heat in resistor R.) Tj
T*
ET

