(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the transient charging and discharging of a capacitor in a series R-C circuit excited by a DC voltage source.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   DC Transient Analysis of Series R-C Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   1. Capacitor Charging:) Tj
T*
(   - Series R and uncharged capacitor C connected to DC voltage V at t = 0 \(vc\(0\) = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - KVL: V = R * i\(t\) + vc\(t\). Since i\(t\) = C * dvc/dt:) Tj
T*
(   R * C * dvc/dt + vc\(t\) = V => dvc/dt + vc / \(RC\) = V / \(RC\).) Tj
T*
(   - General solution: vc\(t\) = V + K * exp\(-t / RC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Applying vc\(0\) = 0 => K = -V.) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor Voltage:) Tj
T*
(   vc\(t\) = V * [ 1 - exp\(- t / tau\) ], where tau = R * C is the capacitive time constant.) Tj
T*
(   - Charging Current:) Tj
T*
(   i\(t\) = C * dvc/dt = \(V / R\) * exp\(- t / tau\).) Tj
T*
(   - At t = tau: vc\(tau\) = 0.632 * V, and current drops to 36.8% of initial value V/R.) Tj
T*
(   - Total energy drawn from supply = Integral\(V * i dt\) = C * V^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Energy stored in electrostatic field = 0.5 * C * V^2. Exactly 50% is lost as heat in resistor) Tj
T*
(   R regardless of the value of R!) Tj
T*
(   2. Capacitor Discharging:) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor charged to initial voltage V0 discharged through resistor R:) Tj
T*
(   R * C * dvc/dt + vc = 0 => vc\(t\) = V0 * exp\(- t / tau\).) Tj
T*
(   - Discharge current: i\(t\) = - \(V0 / R\) * exp\(- t / tau\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
