(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate and solve the second-order differential equation for a series R-L-C circuit, analyzing overdamped, critically damped, and underdamped cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Second-Order Dynamics of Series R-L-C Circuits:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Differential Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - KVL around series loop: L * d^2 q/dt^2 + R * dq/dt + q/C = V.) Tj
T*
(   - In terms of current i\(t\) = dq/dt:) Tj
T*
(   d^2 i/dt^2 + \(R / L\) * di/dt + [1 / \(L * C\)] * i = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Standard form: d^2 i/dt^2 + 2 * alpha * di/dt + omega_0^2 * i = 0, where:) Tj
T*
(   * Damping coefficient: alpha = R / \(2 * L\).) Tj
T*
(   * Undamped natural frequency: omega_0 = 1 / sqrt\(L * C\).) Tj
T*
(   * Damping ratio: zeta = alpha / omega_0 = \(R / 2\) * sqrt\(C / L\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Characteristic Roots:) Tj
T*
(   - s1, s2 = - alpha +- sqrt\( alpha^2 - omega_0^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   3. Three Dynamic Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: Overdamped \(alpha > omega_0, zeta > 1, R > 2*sqrt\(L/C\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Roots are distinct, negative real numbers.) Tj
T*
(   Response: i\(t\) = A1 * exp\(s1*t\) + A2 * exp\(s2*t\). Sluggish, non-oscillatory return to) Tj
T*
(   equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: Critically Damped \(alpha = omega_0, zeta = 1, R = 2*sqrt\(L/C\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Roots are equal, negative real numbers \(s1 = s2 = -alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   Response: i\(t\) = \(A1 + A2 * t\) * exp\(-alpha*t\). Fastest possible return to steady state without) Tj
T*
(   overshoot.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 3: Underdamped \(alpha < omega_0, zeta < 1, R < 2*sqrt\(L/C\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Roots are complex conjugate pairs: s1,2 = -alpha +- j * omega_d, where damped frequency omega_d) Tj
T*
(   = sqrt\(omega_0^2 - alpha^2\).) Tj
T*
ET

