/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Ferranti Effect in AC Transmission Lines, providing mathematical derivation and mitigation methods.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ferranti Effect in Long AC Transmission Lines:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Phenomenon:) Tj
T*
(   - When a long, lightly loaded or open-circuited AC transmission line is energized, the voltage) Tj
T*
(   at the receiving end \(V_R\) rises significantly above the voltage at the sending end \(V_S\): V_R) Tj
T*
(   > V_S.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation via Distributed Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Line parameters: Series impedance z = r + j*omega*L; Shunt admittance y = j*omega*C.) Tj
T*
(   - ABCD two-port transmission line matrix:) Tj
T*
(   V_S = A * V_R + B * I_R.) Tj
T*
(   - Under open-circuit receiving conditions \(I_R = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   V_S = A * V_R => V_R = V_S / A.) Tj
T*
(   - For a short-to-medium nominal-pi line:) Tj
T*
(   A = 1 + \(Z * Y\) / 2 = 1 + \(j*omega*L\) * \(j*omega*C\) / 2 = 1 - \(omega^2 * L * C\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Since omega^2 * L * C > 0:) Tj
T*
(   A < 1 \(e.g., A = 0.95\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   V_R = V_S / [1 - \(omega^2 * L * C\) / 2] > V_S.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage Rise: Delta-V = V_R - V_S approx V_S * \(omega^2 * L * C\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Physical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Large line charging current \(I_C = j*omega*C * V_R\) flows through the series inductive) Tj
T*
(   reactance \(j*omega*L\). The resulting voltage drop across the inductance is:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-V_L = I_C * \(j*omega*L\) = \(j*omega*C * V_R\) * \(j*omega*L\) = - omega^2 * L * C * V_R.) Tj
T*
(   - Because j * j = -1, this drop is 180 degrees out of phase with normal inductive drops,) Tj
T*
(   effectively boosting receiving voltage.) Tj
T*
(   4. Mitigation Techniques:) Tj
T*
(   - Installation of Shunt Reactors \(inductive coils\) at receiving-end substations to absorb) Tj
T*
(   excess capacitive charging VARs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
