(   - Initial load state:) Tj
T*
(   Active Power: P.) Tj
T*
(   Initial Power Factor: cos\(phi1\) => Initial Reactive Power Q1 = P * tan\(phi1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Target compensated state:) Tj
T*
(   Target Power Factor: cos\(phi2\) => New Net Reactive Power Q2 = P * tan\(phi2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Required Reactive Power supplied by Shunt Capacitor Bank:) Tj
T*
(   Q_C = Q1 - Q2 = P * [ tan\(phi1\) - tan\(phi2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Capacitor Sizing \(Single-Phase\):) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive power generated by capacitor across voltage V at frequency omega = 2*pi*f:) Tj
T*
(   Q_C = V^2 / XC = V^2 * \(omega * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equating expressions:) Tj
T*
(   C = Q_C / \(2 * pi * f * V^2\) = P * [ tan\(phi1\) - tan\(phi2\) ] / [ 2 * pi * f * V^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   4. 3-Phase Bank Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - For a Delta-connected capacitor bank across line voltage V_L:) Tj
T*
(   C_delta = Q_C / [ 3 * 2 * pi * f * V_L^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Delta connection requires 1/3 the capacitance of a Star connection for identical kVAR rating) Tj
T*
(   because each unit operates at full line voltage V_L rather than phase voltage V_L / sqrt\(3\).) Tj
