(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze an AC circuit problem: Calculate total current, power, and power factor for a parallel R-L and R-C network.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Numerical Analysis of Parallel AC Network:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Statement:) Tj
T*
(   - A 230 V, 50 Hz single-phase supply is connected across two parallel branches:) Tj
T*
(   Branch 1: Resistor R1 = 12 Ohms in series with inductor L1 = 0.05 H.) Tj
T*
(   Branch 2: Resistor R2 = 20 Ohms in series with capacitor C2 = 100 microfarads.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1: Branch Impedances and Admittances:) Tj
T*
(   - Angular frequency: omega = 2 * pi * 50 = 314.16 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Branch 1:) Tj
T*
(   XL1 = omega * L1 = 314.16 * 0.05 = 15.71 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   Z1 = 12 + j*15.71 Ohms = 19.77 /_ 52.6 deg Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   Y1 = 1 / Z1 = 0.0506 /_ -52.6 deg = \(0.0307 - j*0.0402\) S.) Tj
T*
(   - Branch 2:) Tj
T*
(   XC2 = 1 / \(omega * C2\) = 1 / \(314.16 * 100 * 10^-6\) = 31.83 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   Z2 = 20 - j*31.83 Ohms = 37.60 /_ -57.86 deg Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   Y2 = 1 / Z2 = 0.0266 /_ +57.86 deg = \(0.0141 + j*0.0225\) S.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2: Total Admittance and Current:) Tj
T*
(   - Y_total = Y1 + Y2 = \(0.0307 + 0.0141\) + j*\(-0.0402 + 0.0225\) = 0.0448 - j*0.0177 S.) Tj
T*
(   - Polar form: |Y_total| = sqrt\(0.0448^2 + \(-0.0177\)^2\) = 0.0482 S; theta = arctan\(-0.0177 /) Tj
T*
(   0.0448\) = -21.55 deg.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Line Current:) Tj
T*
(   I_total = V * Y_total = 230 * 0.0482 = 11.08 A.) Tj
T*
(   4. Step 3: Power and Power Factor:) Tj
T*
(   - Power Factor: cos\(21.55 deg\) = 0.930 lagging \(since net susceptance is negative/inductive\).) Tj
T*
(   - Active Power: P = V * I * cos\(phi\) = 230 * 11.08 * 0.930 = 2370 Watts \(2.37 kW\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive Power: Q = V * I * sin\(phi\) = 230 * 11.08 * sin\(21.55 deg\) = 936 VAR.) Tj
T*
