(   AC Transient Analysis of Series R-L Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   1. Differential Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - L * di/dt + R * i\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t + alpha\), with switch closed at t = 0 \(i\(0\) = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   2. General Solution \(Complementary Function + Particular Integral\):) Tj
T*
(   - Natural / Transient Response \(CF\):) Tj
T*
(   i_tr\(t\) = K * exp\(- R*t / L\).) Tj
T*
(   - Steady-State Response \(PI\):) Tj
T*
(   i_ss\(t\) = \(Vm / |Z|\) * sin\(omega * t + alpha - theta\),) Tj
T*
(   where |Z| = sqrt\(R^2 + omega^2*L^2\) and impedance angle theta = arctan\(omega*L / R\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total current:) Tj
T*
(   i\(t\) = K * exp\(- R*t / L\) + \(Vm / |Z|\) * sin\(omega * t + alpha - theta\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Evaluation of Constant K from Initial Condition i\(0\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   - 0 = K + \(Vm / |Z|\) * sin\(alpha - theta\) => K = - \(Vm / |Z|\) * sin\(alpha - theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Complete Analytical Solution:) Tj
T*
(   i\(t\) = \(Vm / |Z|\) * [ sin\(omega*t + alpha - theta\) - sin\(alpha - theta\) * exp\(- R*t / L\) ].) Tj
T*
(   4. Physical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - Case A \(Zero Transient\): If circuit is switched at angle alpha such that alpha - theta = 0 or) Tj
T*
(   pi, sin\(alpha - theta\) = 0. The DC transient term vanishes identically; current enters steady) Tj
T*
(   state immediately!) Tj
T*
(   - Case B \(Maximum Doubling Transient\): If switched when alpha - theta = -pi/2, sin\(alpha -) Tj
T*
(   theta\) = -1. The DC offset is maximum: K = +Vm / |Z|. After a half-cycle, peak current) Tj
T*
(   approaches nearly 2 * \(Vm / |Z|\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
