BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Harmonics in AC power systems, defining Total Harmonic Distortion \(THD\), Crest Factor, and Triplen harmonics in 3-phase circuits.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Harmonics and Waveform Distortion in AC Systems:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fourier Series Representation:) Tj
T*
(   - Any periodic distorted non-sinusoidal voltage/current waveform can be decomposed into an) Tj
T*
(   infinite series:) Tj
T*
(   f\(t\) = a0/2 + Sum_{n=1}^infinity [ an * cos\(n*omega*t\) + bn * sin\(n*omega*t\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - n = 1 is the Fundamental component \(50 Hz\).) Tj
T*
(   - n = 2, 3, 4, ... are Harmonic components of frequency n * f1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Total Harmonic Distortion \(THD\):) Tj
T*
(   - Measure of distortion relative to the fundamental:) Tj
T*
(   THD_V = sqrt\( Sum_{n=2}^infinity V_n^2 \) / V_1.) Tj
T*
(   THD_I = sqrt\( Sum_{n=2}^infinity I_n^2 \) / I_1.) Tj
T*
(   - IEEE 519 standard strictly limits voltage THD to < 5% at point of common coupling.) Tj
T*
(   3. Triplen Harmonics in 3-Phase Systems:) Tj
T*
(   - Harmonics that are integer multiples of 3 \(n = 3, 9, 15, ...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Phase displacement between triplen harmonics in adjacent phases:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-theta = 3 * 120 deg = 360 deg = 0 deg.) Tj
T*
(   - Triplens are co-phasal!) Tj
T*
(   - Consequence:) Tj
T*
(   * In 3-phase 4-wire systems, third harmonic currents add directly in the neutral wire: I_N\(3rd\)) Tj
T*
(   = 3 * I_ph\(3rd\). Neutral conductor can severely overheat.) Tj
T*
(   * In Delta windings, triplen harmonics circulate around the closed loop and cannot escape into) Tj
T*
(   the external transmission lines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
