(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the step response of an uncharged capacitor energized through an inductor and resistor \(Series R-L-C step response\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step Response of Series R-L-C Circuit \(Capacitor Voltage\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Formulation in s-Domain \(Laplace Transform\):) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit energized by step DC voltage V*u\(t\) with zero initial conditions \(vc\(0\) = 0, i\(0\) =) Tj
T*
(   0\).) Tj
T*
(   - s-domain loop equation:) Tj
T*
(   V\(s\) = V / s = I\(s\) * [ R + s*L + 1/\(s*C\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Current: I\(s\) = \(V / L\) / [ s^2 + \(R/L\)*s + 1/\(LC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor voltage Vc\(s\) = I\(s\) / \(s*C\):) Tj
T*
(   Vc\(s\) = \(V / LC\) / [ s * \( s^2 + 2*alpha*s + omega_0^2 \) ],) Tj
T*
(   where alpha = R / \(2*L\) and omega_0^2 = 1 / \(LC\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Inverse Laplace Transform for Underdamped Case \(alpha < omega_0\):) Tj
T*
(   - Partial fraction expansion yields:) Tj
T*
(   vc\(t\) = V * [ 1 - exp\(-alpha*t\) * \( cos\(omega_d*t\) + \(alpha / omega_d\) * sin\(omega_d*t\) \) ],) Tj
T*
(   where omega_d = sqrt\(omega_0^2 - alpha^2\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Physical Behavior and Peak Overshoot:) Tj
T*
(   - The capacitor voltage does NOT stop at supply voltage V.) Tj
T*
(   - Due to energy transfer between the magnetic field of L and electric field of C, vc\(t\)) Tj
T*
(   overshoots to a maximum value at t_peak = pi / omega_d:) Tj
T*
(   vc\(t_peak\) = V * [ 1 + exp\(- alpha * pi / omega_d\) ] = V * [ 1 + exp\(- pi * zeta / sqrt\(1 -) Tj
T*
(   zeta^2\)\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - For a lossless circuit \(R = 0, zeta = 0\), peak voltage reaches exactly 2 * V \(100%) Tj
T*
(   overshoot\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
