BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Complex Power in terms of Voltage and Current Phasors, defining Apparent, Active, Reactive, and Distortion Power.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Complex Power Formulation and Non-Sinusoidal Distortions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Complex Power \(S\):) Tj
T*
(   - For voltage phasor V = |V| /_ alpha and current phasor I = |I| /_ beta:) Tj
T*
(   Complex power is defined as:) Tj
T*
(   S = V * I* \(where I* is the complex conjugate of I\).) Tj
T*
(   - S = |V| /_ alpha * |I| /_ -beta = |V| * |I| /_ \(alpha - beta\) = |V| * |I| /_ phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Euler expansion:) Tj
T*
(   S = |V| * |I| * cos\(phi\) + j * |V| * |I| * sin\(phi\) = P + j * Q.) Tj
T*
(   - Active Power: P = Re{S} = |V| * |I| * cos\(phi\) [Watts].) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive Power: Q = Im{S} = |V| * |I| * sin\(phi\) [VAR].) Tj
T*
(   - Taking the conjugate of I ensures that lagging inductive current \(beta < alpha, phi > 0\)) Tj
T*
(   produces positive reactive power \(+jQ\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Distorted \(Non-Sinusoidal\) Power \(Budeanu's Formulation\):) Tj
T*
(   - When harmonics are present:) Tj
T*
(   P = Sum_{n=1}^infinity V_n * I_n * cos\(phi_n\).) Tj
T*
(   Q = Sum_{n=1}^infinity V_n * I_n * sin\(phi_n\).) Tj
T*
(   Apparent Power: S = V_rms * I_rms.) Tj
T*
(   - In distorted systems: S^2 > P^2 + Q^2.) Tj
T*
(   - The discrepancy is termed Distortion Power D:) Tj
T*
(   S = sqrt\( P^2 + Q^2 + D^2 \).) Tj
