BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Two-Wattmeter readings under different load power factors \(Unity, 0.866, 0.5, 0, and leading power factor\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comprehensive Analysis of Two-Wattmeter Readings Across Power Factors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Equations:) Tj
T*
(   - W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(30 deg - phi\)) Tj
T*
(   - W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(30 deg + phi\)) Tj
T*
(   2. Case Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: Unity Power Factor \(phi = 0 deg, cos phi = 1.0\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(30\) = 0.866 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(30\) = 0.866 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   Both meters read positive and identical values \(W1 = W2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: 0.866 Lagging Power Factor \(phi = 30 deg, cos phi = 0.866\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(0\) = V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(60\) = 0.5 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W1 = 2 * W2 \(W1 reads twice W2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 3: 0.5 Lagging Power Factor \(phi = 60 deg, cos phi = 0.5\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(-30\) = 0.866 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(90\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Wattmeter W2 reads zero! All 3-phase power is registered exclusively by W1.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 4: Power Factor < 0.5 Lagging \(e.g., phi = 75 deg, cos phi = 0.259\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(-45\) = +0.707 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(105\) = -0.259 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   Wattmeter W2 deflects backward \(negative reading\). To read W2, its pressure coil leads must be) Tj
T*
(   reversed, and reading subtracted: P = W1 - W2.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 5: Zero Power Factor \(phi = 90 deg, cos phi = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   W1 = V_L * I_L * cos\(-60\) = +0.5 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
(   W2 = V_L * I_L * cos\(120\) = -0.5 * V_L * I_L.) Tj
T*
