(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Phase Sequence and phase sequence indicators \(rotating disc type and static lamp type\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Phase Sequence and Detection Methods:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - Phase sequence is the order in which the 3-phase voltages attain their positive peak values) Tj
T*
(   \(standard sequence: R-Y-B\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reversal of phase sequence \(e.g., R-B-Y\) reverses the direction of rotation of all 3-phase) Tj
T*
(   induction and synchronous motors, which can cause catastrophic mechanical failure in cranes,) Tj
T*
(   pumps, and elevators.) Tj
T*
(   2. Rotating Disc Phase Sequence Indicator:) Tj
T*
(   - Operates on the induction motor principle.) Tj
T*
(   - Consists of three star-connected electromagnetic coils spaced 120 degrees apart around a) Tj
T*
(   pivoted aluminum disc.) Tj
T*
(   - When connected to the 3-phase supply, the coils produce a rotating magnetic field that) Tj
T*
(   induces eddy currents in the disc.) Tj
T*
(   - If sequence is R-Y-B, disc rotates in the arrow direction \(clockwise\). If sequence is) Tj
T*
(   reversed, disc rotates counterclockwise.) Tj
T*
(   3. Static Lamp-Capacitor Phase Sequence Indicator:) Tj
T*
(   - Consists of two incandescent lamps \(L1, L2\) and one capacitor C connected in star across the) Tj
T*
(   3-phase terminals \(R, Y, B\).) Tj
T*
(   - Due to the 90 degree phase shift introduced by the capacitor, the neutral displacement causes) Tj
T*
(   unequal voltages across the two lamps:) Tj
T*
(   One lamp glows brilliantly, while the other lamp remains dim or completely dark.) Tj
T*
(   - If lamp connected to line Y is bright, sequence is R-Y-B; if lamp on line B is bright,) Tj
T*
(   sequence is R-B-Y.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
