(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the frequency response, cut-off frequencies, and bandwidth of a parallel resonant circuit with high Q.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Frequency Response of Parallel Resonant Tank:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Model and Input Admittance:) Tj
T*
(   - Parallel combination of ideal capacitor C, inductor L, and equivalent shunt resistance R_p:) Tj
T*
(   Y\(omega\) = 1/R_p + j * [ omega * C - 1 / \(omega * L\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - At resonance \(omega_0 = 1 / sqrt\(LC\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Y\(omega_0\) = 1 / R_p => Z\(omega_0\) = R_p \(Maximum real impedance\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Deviation from Resonance \(High-Q Approximation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Let omega = omega_0 + Delta-omega.) Tj
T*
(   - Net susceptance:) Tj
T*
(   B\(omega\) approx 2 * C * Delta-omega.) Tj
T*
(   - Total admittance:) Tj
T*
(   Y\(omega\) = \(1 / R_p\) * [ 1 + j * 2 * R_p * C * Delta-omega ] = \(1 / R_p\) * [ 1 + j * 2 * Q *) Tj
T*
(   \(Delta-omega / omega_0\) ],) Tj
T*
(   where Q = R_p * omega_0 * C = R_p / \(omega_0 * L\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Cut-Off \(Half-Power\) Frequencies:) Tj
T*
(   - Occur when the magnitude of impedance drops to R_p / sqrt\(2\) \(admittance increases by) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(2\)\):) Tj
T*
(   2 * Q * \(Delta-omega / omega_0\) = +- 1 => Delta-omega = +- omega_0 / \(2 * Q\).) Tj
T*
