(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze an AC bridge: Maxwell's Inductance-Capacitance Bridge, deriving balance equations for L and R.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Maxwell's Inductance-Capacitance Bridge Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Bridge Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 1 \(AB\): Known standard capacitor C1 in parallel with known variable resistor R1.) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 2 \(BC\): Known non-inductive variable resistor R2.) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 3 \(CD\): Known non-inductive resistor R3.) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 4 \(DA\): Unknown inductive coil having resistance Rx and inductance Lx.) Tj
T*
(   - AC source of frequency omega connected across AC; detector across BD.) Tj
T*
(   2. Balance Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - At balance, detector current is zero: Zx * Y1 = R2 / R3 => Zx = R2 * R3 * Y1.) Tj
T*
(   - Impedance of Arm 4: Zx = Rx + j * omega * Lx.) Tj
T*
(   - Admittance of Arm 1: Y1 = 1 / R1 + j * omega * C1.) Tj
T*
(   - Equating:) Tj
T*
(   Rx + j * omega * Lx = R2 * R3 * [ \(1 / R1\) + j * omega * C1 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Separation of Real and Imaginary Parts:) Tj
T*
(   - Real Part:) Tj
T*
(   Rx = \(R2 * R3\) / R1.) Tj
T*
(   - Imaginary Part:) Tj
T*
(   omega * Lx = omega * C1 * R2 * R3 => Lx = C1 * R2 * R3.) Tj
T*
(   4. Salient Features:) Tj
T*
(   - Both balance equations are completely independent of source frequency omega.) Tj
T*
(   - Unknown coil inductance Lx is measured directly in terms of standard capacitor C1.) Tj
T*
(   - Ideal for measuring medium-Q coils \(1 < Q < 10\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
