(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Schering's Bridge for precision measurement of dielectric capacitance and loss angle \(dissipation factor\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Schering's Bridge for Dielectric Capacitance and Loss Factor:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Objective:) Tj
T*
(   - Precision measurement of capacitance and dielectric loss angle delta \(tan delta, dissipation) Tj
T*
(   factor\) of high-voltage cables and insulators.) Tj
T*
(   2. Bridge Arms:) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 1: Unknown capacitor Cx with series equivalent loss resistance rx \(represented as Zx = rx) Tj
T*
(   - j / \(omega*Cx\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 2: High-voltage, loss-free standard air/gas capacitor C2.) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 3: Non-inductive resistor R3.) Tj
T*
(   - Arm 4: Variable resistor R4 in parallel with variable capacitor C4.) Tj
T*
(   3. Balance Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Zx / R3 = Z2 * Y4 => Zx = R3 * Z2 * Y4.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute expressions:) Tj
T*
(   rx - j / \(omega * Cx\) = R3 * [ -j / \(omega * C2\) ] * [ \(1 / R4\) + j * omega * C4 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply through:) Tj
T*
(   rx - j / \(omega * Cx\) = \(R3 * C4\) / C2 - j * [ R3 / \(omega * C2 * R4\) ].) Tj
T*
(   4. Separation of Components:) Tj
T*
(   - Equating real parts:) Tj
T*
(   rx = R3 * \(C4 / C2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equating imaginary parts:) Tj
T*
(   1 / \(omega * Cx\) = R3 / \(omega * C2 * R4\) => Cx = C2 * \(R4 / R3\).) Tj
T*
(   5. Dissipation Factor \(tan delta\):) Tj
T*
(   - tan\(delta\) = omega * Cx * rx = omega * [ C2 * \(R4 / R3\) ] * [ R3 * \(C4 / C2\) ] = omega * C4 *) Tj
T*
(   R4.) Tj
T*
(   - Independent of R3 and C2; directly calibrated via C4 scale.) Tj
