(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the phenomenon of Inrush Current in Power Transformers during AC energization.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Transformer Magnetizing Inrush Current:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - When an unloaded transformer is energized by sinusoidal voltage v\(t\) = Vm * sin\(omega * t +) Tj
T*
(   alpha\), Faraday's law dictates that core flux phi\(t\) is the integral of applied voltage:) Tj
T*
(   phi\(t\) = \(1 / N\) * Integral v\(t\) dt = - \(Vm / omega*N\) * cos\(omega*t + alpha\) + C.) Tj
T*
(   2. Worst-Case Closing Angle \(alpha = 0, Voltage Zero Crossing\):) Tj
T*
(   - If switched at voltage zero \(alpha = 0\) with zero initial residual flux:) Tj
T*
(   phi\(t\) = - phi_m * cos\(omega * t\) + C.) Tj
T*
(   - Since flux cannot change instantaneously \(phi\(0\) = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   0 = - phi_m + C => C = phi_m.) Tj
T*
(   - Resulting Flux Waveform:) Tj
T*
(   phi\(t\) = phi_m * [ 1 - cos\(omega * t\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - At omega*t = pi \(half-cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   phi_peak = 2 * phi_m \(Double the normal peak working flux!\).) Tj
T*
(   - If residual flux phi_r exists from previous de-energization, peak flux reaches:) Tj
T*
(   phi_max = 2 * phi_m + phi_r.) Tj
T*
(   3. Consequences of Ferromagnetic Saturation:) Tj
T*
(   - Transformer cores are designed to operate just below the saturation knee \(~1.5 to 1.7 Tesla\).) Tj
T*
(   - Driving the flux to 2.5 times phi_m forces the core deep into hard saturation where) Tj
T*
(   permeability mu_r drops toward mu_0 \(air\).) Tj
T*
(   - The magnetizing current drawn from the line spikes violently to 10 to 20 times normal rated) Tj
T*
(   full-load current.) Tj
T*
(   - Contains large second-harmonic content, requiring harmonic restraint relays in differential) Tj
T*
(   protection.) Tj
T*
