(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Power Invariance in Symmetrical Components:) Tj
T*
(   1. Total Instantaneous 3-Phase Power in Phase Coordinates:) Tj
T*
(   - Complex power: S_3ph = Va * Ia* + Vb * Ib* + Vc * Ic* = [V_abc]^T * [I_abc]*.) Tj
T*
(   2. Substitution of Symmetrical Component Transformation:) Tj
T*
(   - Let [A] be the Fortescue symmetrical component transformation matrix:) Tj
T*
(   [V_abc] = [A] * [V_012], and [I_abc] = [A] * [I_012].) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   S_3ph = \([A] * [V_012]\)^T * \([A] * [I_012]\)* = [V_012]^T * [A]^T * [A]* * [I_012]*.) Tj
T*
(   3. Evaluation of [A]^T * [A]*:) Tj
T*
(   - [A] = [ 1 1 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 a^2 a ]) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 a a^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluating product:) Tj
T*
(   [A]^T * [A]* = 3 * [I] \(where [I] is 3x3 identity matrix\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Power Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - S_3ph = 3 * [V_012]^T * [I_012]* = 3 * \( Va0 * Ia0* + Va1 * Ia1* + Va2 * Ia2* \).) Tj
T*
(   - Active Power: P_3ph = 3 * [ Va0*Ia0*cos\(phi0\) + Va1*Ia1*cos\(phi1\) + Va2*Ia2*cos\(phi2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Reactive Power: Q_3ph = 3 * [ Va0*Ia0*sin\(phi0\) + Va1*Ia1*sin\(phi1\) + Va2*Ia2*sin\(phi2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Power Invariance Factor: The factor of 3 arises because standard Fortescue transformation is) Tj
T*
(   non-unitary; dividing [A] by sqrt\(3\) yields power-invariant unitary matrices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

